  "summary": "rrs exfiltrates screenshots and host identifiers to a hardcoded Discord webhook on CLI launch",
  "details": "The package advertises itself as a P2P chat client. On running the `rrs` CLI, `rrs/__main__.py:main` starts `run_capture` in a daemon thread before the GUI appears. `capture.py` uses `mss` to grab a full-screen screenshot of `sct.monitors[0]`, collects the machine hostname and username, and POSTs the PNG together with these identifiers to a hardcoded Discord webhook at `https://discord.com/api/webhooks/1549807268294303860/...`. The screen capture and upload are not documented, are not gated behind any consent prompt or configuration, and are unrelated to the advertised chat functionality.",
